#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Privileged owner of the installer screen's state on the installation ISO.

The kiosk on tty1 (cybexos-installer) is an unprivileged, stateless renderer.
It connects to this daemon's Unix socket, receives bounded JSON state
snapshots and sends requests. This daemon keeps the draft plan, Wi-Fi,
time zone detection, keyboard layout and diagnostics, and drives the one
disk-writing worker, `cybexos-install --json-ui`, over its unchanged private
stdin/stdout protocol. A screen restart (keyboard change, crash, Ctrl+Alt+
Backspace) resumes on the same step; the installation itself keeps running.

Passwords are held in memory only between review and the final click, are
sent to the worker only with the reviewed token, and never appear in a
snapshot, log line or argument.
"""
